 ```toml
 [dependencies]
-whippyalgebra = { version = "0.1", default-features = false, features = ["std"] }
+whippyalgebra = { version = "0.1", default-features = false, features = ["std", "standalone-indexing"] }
 ```
+
+Backend-free builds must explicitly enable `standalone-indexing` when default
+features are disabled. This retains the existing `Nat<N>` / `ShapeIndex` API
+and typenum's full supported index domain. A bare `--no-default-features` build
+now reports a configuration error until either this feature or `nalgebra` is
+enabled. The feature is enabled by default for compatibility; another dependency
+can enable it through Cargo feature unification even in a reduced nalgebra build.
 
